From 3bb0aad827f4c36d1a9ab5d9c0bfd21c47ab7cea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Da Bi <isayama@Das-iMac.local>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 16:20:22 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Fix use-after-free / data race on cell->stars.sort
 (on-the-fly stars sort lock + deferred free)

The stars feedback DOSUB path (runner_dosub_pair_stars_feedback) triggers
runner_do_stars_sort() on the fly, outside the task graph. Unlike the hydro
equivalent (runner_do_hydro_sort, called with lock=1), the stars sort took no
lock, so two runner threads could concurrently (re)sort the same cell and race
inside cell_malloc_stars_sorts() -> one swift_free()s c->stars.sort while the
other memcpy/walks it -> SIGSEGV in runner_do_stars_sort.

Mirror the hydro.sort fix for stars.sort:
- Add a per-cell stars.extra_sort_lock (+ init in space.c/space_regrid.c,
  destroy in space_recycle.c).
- Give runner_do_stars_sort() a `lock` parameter with the same double-checked
  locking as the hydro sort; pass lock=1 from the four on-the-fly feedback
  call sites, lock=0 from the scheduled stars_sort task and runner_do_all_stars_sort
  (already serialised by task dependencies).
- Defer freeing grown-over stars.sort buffers (cell_retire_stars_sort /
  cell_free_retired_stars_sorts, freed at the rebuild barrier from
  space_rebuild) so concurrent feedback readers cannot use-after-free.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014QEuoaGLV1UoeayXpF6SvQ
